  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature that is equipped is considered modified no matter who controls the Equipment that's attached to it.",
      "oracle_id": "722ab6e4-a2e0-4aaa-a050-7b6436e22b40",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature with a counter on it is considered modified no matter what kind of counter it is or which player put it on that creature.",
      "oracle_id": "722ab6e4-a2e0-4aaa-a050-7b6436e22b40",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An Aura controlled by an opponent does not cause a creature you control to be modified.",
      "oracle_id": "722ab6e4-a2e0-4aaa-a050-7b6436e22b40",
      "published_at": "2025-09-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature that is equipped is considered modified no matter who controls the Equipment that's attached to it.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature with a counter on it is considered modified no matter what kind of counter it is or which player put it on that creature.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A permanent that turns face up or face down changes characteristics but is otherwise the same permanent. Spells and abilities that were targeting that permanent and Auras and Equipment that were attached to that permanent aren't affected unless the new characteristics of the object change the legality of those targets or attachments.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An Aura controlled by another player does not cause a creature you control to be modified.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any time you have priority, you may turn a manifested creature face up by revealing that it's a creature card (ignoring any copy effects or type-changing effects that might be applying to it) and paying its mana cost. This is a special action. It doesn't use the stack and can't be responded to.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because face-down creatures don't have a name, they can't have the same name as any other creature, even another face-down creature.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because the permanent is on the battlefield both before and after it's turned face up, turning a permanent face up doesn't cause any enters-the-battlefield abilities to trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a double-faced card is manifested, it will be put onto the battlefield face down. While face down, it can't transform. If the front face of the card is a creature card, you can turn it face up by paying its mana cost. If you do, its front face will be up.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a face-down permanent leaves the battlefield, you must reveal it. You must also reveal all face-down spells and permanents you control if you leave the game or the game end.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a manifested creature would have morph or disguise if it were face up, you may also turn it face up by paying its morph cost or disguise cost.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If something tries to turn a face-down instant or sorcery card on the battlefield face up, reveal that card to show all players it's an instant or sorcery card. The permanent remains on the battlefield face down. Abilities that trigger when a permanent turns face up won't trigger, because even though you revealed the card, it never turned face up.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To manifest a card, put it onto the battlefield face down. It becomes a 2/2 face-down creature card with no name, mana cost, or creature types. It's colorless and has a mana value of 0. Other effects that apply to the permanent can still grant it any characteristics it doesn't have or change the characteristics it does have.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turning a permanent face up or face down doesn't change whether that permanent is tapped or untapped.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Unlike a face-down creature that was cast using a morph or disguise ability, a manifested creature may still be turned face up after it loses its abilities if it's a creature card.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must ensure that your face-down spells and permanents can be easily differentiated from each other. You're not allowed to mix up the cards that represent them on the battlefield to confuse other players. The order in which they entered the battlefield should remain clear, as well as what ability caused them to be face down. (This includes morph, manifest, disguise, cloak, and a few other effects that turn cards face down.) Common methods for doing this include using markers or dice, or simply placing them in order on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "89b88a6c-92be-43eb-9de4-f79cc75c6d90",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Equipped creatures will get just +1/+1 from Stone Haven Outfitter, no matter how many Equipment are attached to them. Similarly, the last ability will trigger just once per equipped creature.",
      "oracle_id": "8e646a6b-77ba-4f7d-8ee9-b0b084453f77",
      "published_at": "2016-01-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this context, \"equipped creatures you control\" and \"equipped creature you control\" refer to any creatures you control with Equipment attached to them. In the highly unusual case that Stone Haven Outfitter becomes an Equipment, the meaning of its abilities doesn't change. The bonuses continue to refer to any equipped creature you control. They aren't bonuses applied solely to the creature Stone Haven Outfitter is attached to.",
      "oracle_id": "8e646a6b-77ba-4f7d-8ee9-b0b084453f77",
      "published_at": "2016-01-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The bonuses gained from Stone Haven Outfitter's abilities are in addition to any bonuses given by the Equipment.",
      "oracle_id": "8e646a6b-77ba-4f7d-8ee9-b0b084453f77",
      "published_at": "2016-01-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A permanent can have multiple Roles attached to it if each one is controlled by a different player.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Cards in the Wilds of Eldraine main set create six different Role tokens: Cursed, Monster, Royal, Sorcerer, Wicked, and Young Hero. A seventh Role token, Virtuous, is created by Ellivere of the Wild Court, the commander of the \"Virtue and Valor\" Commander Deck.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Hexproof and shroud won't prevent a Role from becoming attached to a permanent if the ability creating that Role attached to that permanent doesn't target it.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a permanent has more than one Role attached to it controlled by the same player, each of those Roles except the one with the most recent timestamp is put into its owner's graveyard. This is a state-based action.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more Roles controlled by the same player become attached to a permanent at the same time (perhaps due to an effect such as that of Doubling Season), that player chooses which one to keep and which are put into their owners' graveyards.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In rare cases, a spell or ability might attempt to create a Role token enchanting a permanent that it can't legally enchant (because of an ability like protection from enchantments). In such cases, the Role token isn't created.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Roles are colorless enchantment tokens. Each one has the Aura and Role subtypes and the enchant creature ability.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some spells and abilities that create Role tokens require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. The Role token won't be created.",
      "oracle_id": "97f9b82f-b3cf-44ff-9abc-2d92d7cbaa27",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature enters the battlefield under your control and gains haste, but then loses it before attacking, it won't be able to attack that turn. This means that you can't use one Lightning Greaves to allow two new creatures to attack in the same turn.",
      "oracle_id": "ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't simply unequip Equipment from a creature. If Lightning Greaves is attached to the only creature you control, you won't be able to attach other equipment to it (or target it with anything else) until you have another creature to which you can attach Lightning Greaves.",
      "oracle_id": "ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gaining control of a permanent doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.",
      "oracle_id": "d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gaining control of an Aura or Equipment doesn't change what it's attached to.",
      "oracle_id": "d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gaining control of a permanent doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.",
      "oracle_id": "d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gaining control of an Aura or Equipment doesn't change what it's attached to.",
      "oracle_id": "d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6",
